<h2>Cardboard Sandwich Wedge Boxes With Clear Viewing Panels</h2>
<p>Sandwich wedge packaging can include a clear front panel to show layers such as chicken, cheese, lettuce, or mixed vegetables while the sandwich remains enclosed. Many sellers use <a href="https://shopcardboardboxes.com/product-category/food-related-cardboard-boxes/"><strong>Food Related Cardboard Boxes</strong></a> when they want sandwich packs aligned with salads, wraps, and snack items in the same display zone. The angled front helps keep the sandwich visible so customers can see the contents without opening the pack.</p>
<p>Clear-view wedge formats support sealed handling while keeping the sandwich visible at the front. Size planning helps match different sandwich heights and reduces movement during transport. This is useful for meal-prep packs that include thicker fillings or multi-layer builds.</p>
<h3>How Clear Windows Support Retail Selection</h3>
<p>A clear front panel helps people recognize the sandwich type on the shelf when several variants are placed next to each other. Fillings and textures can be seen without opening the pack, which reduces contact with the product. It also helps staff keep rows consistent during restocking. In chilled displays, the window keeps the sandwich visible under standard cold-case lighting.</p>
